{"s":"V","updated":"2026-11-28T06:21:30.243482+00:00","profile":{"name":"Visa Inc.","summary":"Visa Inc. operates as a payments technology company in the United States and internationally. It operates VisaNet, a transaction processing network that enables authorization, clearing, and settlement of payment transactions. The company also offers credit, debit, and prepaid card products; tap to pay, tokenization, and click to pay services; Visa Direct, a platform which facilitates money movement, enabling clients to collect, hold, convert, and send funds across its network; and issuing solutions, such as airport lounge access, dining reservations, shopping experiences, event tickets, and seller offers. In addition, it provides acceptance solutions, an omnichannel payment integration with e-commerce platforms; risk detection and prevention solutions; and advisory and other services comprising consulting practice, proprietary analytics models, data scientists and economists, marketing services, and managed services. The company provides its services under the Visa, Visa Electron, V PAY, Interlink, and PLUS brands. It serves consumers, sellers, financial institutions, and government entities. Visa Inc. was founded in 1958 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","industry":"Credit Services","sector":"Financial Services","employees":34800,"address":"300 Toni Stone Crossing, San Francisco, CA 94158, United States","phone":"650 432 7644","website":"https://corporate.visa.com","ir":"http://investor.visa.com/phoenix.zhtml?c=215693&p=irol-IRHome","exchange":"NYSE","officers":[{"n":"Mr. Ryan M. McInerney","t":"CEO & Director","age":50,"pay":7129213},{"n":"Mr. Christopher Suh","t":"Chief Financial Officer","age":55,"pay":3148478},{"n":"Mr. Rajat Taneja","t":"President of Technology","age":61,"pay":4600880},{"n":"Ms. Kelly Mahon Tullier J.D.","t":"Vice Chair, Chief People & Corporate Affairs Officer and Corporate Secretary","age":59,"pay":3162473},{"n":"Mr. Paul D. Fabar